      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "New findings published in 2012 have challenged common beliefs about stable coronary artery disease. Studies have shown that β-blockers and n-3-polyunsaturated fatty acids have no impact on prognosis, that percutaneous coronary intervention is not always the best option, and that women do not have worse cardiovascular outcomes than men."},
